---
source: tests/cli.rs
expression: "format!(\"{short_help}\\n--- LONG ---\\n{long_help}\\n--- TOOL ---\\n{tool_help}\")"
---
Search indexed items and check service health

Usage: my-tools [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  search-items  Searches indexed items
  http-server   Checks service health

Options:
      --input-json <COMMAND>  Read arguments from stdin as JSON
  -h, --help                  Print help (see more with '--help')
  -V, --version               Print version

Output options (before the command):
      --output <MODE>  Choose output format

Use --help for the full reference.

--- LONG ---
Search indexed items and check service health

Search by query and refine results with filters.

Use fast mode for interactive searches.

Usage: my-tools [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  search-items  Searches indexed items
  http-server   Checks service health

Options:
      --input-json <COMMAND>
          Select a command and read its arguments as one complete JSON object from stdin through EOF. Cannot be combined with a subcommand or its argument options.

          Commands: search-items, http-server

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Output options (before the command):
      --output <MODE>
          Choose output format:

          artifacts   Readable text and generated file paths (default)
          structured  JSON data only; requires structured output
          raw         Complete MCP result as JSON, including encoded file data
          binary      Bytes of exactly one image, audio item, or embedded file

          In binary mode, bytes go to stdout and accompanying text goes to stderr.

      --images <MODE>
          Control inline PNG image display:

          auto   Display on recognized compatible terminals (default)
          kitty  Force Kitty image display
          off    Do not display inline images

          Automatic display is disabled for pipes, redirected output, and custom output writers. Files are saved in every mode. Only available with --output artifacts.

      --artifact-dir <DIR>
          Save generated files beneath this directory (default: system temporary directory). Each invocation uses its own directory and prints absolute file paths.

          Only available with --output artifacts.

--- TOOL ---
Searches indexed items

Usage: search-items [OPTIONS] --mode <STRING> --query <STRING>

Options:
      --mode <STRING>
          Search strategy.

          [possible values: fast, thorough]

      --query <STRING>
          Search expression.

      --environment <JSON>
          Process environment. Value is strict JSON (object); JSON strings require quotes.

      --filter-range-min <INTEGER>
          Smallest accepted value. Required when `filter` is activated. Format: int64.

      --filter-range-max <INTEGER>
          Largest accepted value. Format: int64.

      --filter-tags <STRING>
          Labels to include. Repeat this option once per array item; order is preserved.

      --input-json <STRING>
          A property sharing the root adapter option's spelling.

      --limit <INTEGER>
          Optional result limit. Format: uint64. Minimum: 0.

      --recursive [<BOOL>]
          Whether to recurse. Accepts --option, --option=true, or --option=false forms.

          [possible values: true, false]

      --rules <JSON>
          Ordered matching rules. Value is strict JSON (array); JSON strings require quotes.

      --threshold <NUMBER>
          Optional score threshold. Format: double.

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
